# 3. Authentication, Login, Logout & Email Verification

Create a secure authentication system.

Requirements:

- Login page with email and password.
- Logout button.
- Email verification for HR, Receptionist, and Technician accounts.
- Email verification link with a secure, expiring token.
- Resend verification email option.
- Forgot password and password reset.
- Change password.
- Secure session management.
- Role-based redirects after login.
- Protected routes for every role.
- Account activation and deactivation by Admin.
- Show clear errors for invalid credentials and unverified email addresses.
- Do not store passwords in plain text.
- Use a trusted authentication provider or securely implemented server-side authentication.

HR, Receptionist, and Technician must log in using their own verified email addresses.

Admin must be able to create user accounts, assign roles, activate/deactivate accounts, and manage permissions.

Use environment variables for email provider credentials, API keys, database secrets, and other sensitive settings. Never expose secrets in frontend code.

# 4. Separate Role-Based Panels

Create separate dashboard experiences for each role.

## A. Admin Panel

Admin has full access to the entire application.

Admin can:

- Create, edit, approve, and manage service records.
- Manage customers and products.
- Assign technicians and schedules.
- Approve or reject new service requests submitted by technicians.
- Manage quotations and follow-ups.
- Manage payments, expenses, and customer ledgers.
- Review TA/DA claims.
- Generate all reports.
- Manage users and permissions.
- Review activity logs.
- Configure company details, reminders, and notification settings.
- Print and export authorized reports.

Admin can edit all permitted records. Destructive actions must require confirmation and be logged.

## B. HR Panel

HR can view the records and reports permitted by the Admin.

HR functions:

- View technician schedules.
- View service assignments and completion updates.
- View service history and customer follow-up information.
- Record telephone follow-up notes.
- Record customer responses.
- Record the date and time of follow-up.
- Schedule the next follow-up date.
- Assign follow-up responsibility when authorized.
- View quotation follow-up status.
- View authorized TA/DA reports.
- Generate date-range reports for accessible information.

HR must not automatically receive permission to edit financial records, change service assignments, delete data, or access restricted information.

## C. Receptionist Panel

Receptionists need a simplified, professional interface.

Receptionists can:

- Search customers by name, phone number, or Service ID.
- View customer service history.
- View service status.
- Check whether a product is ready for delivery.
- View pending, delivered, and returned services.
- View today's technician schedules.
- View authorized technician work updates.
- Call customers to provide updates.
- Record customer communication notes.
- Record customer responses and next follow-up dates.
- View quotation status and authorized follow-up information.
- Print authorized service receipts and reports.
- Register new customers and service requests if permitted.

Receptionists must not edit technical findings, change technician assignments, approve service schedules, or modify financial transactions unless Admin grants specific permission.

## D. Technician Panel

Technicians must have their own secure login and dashboard.

Technicians can:

- View only their assigned schedules.
- View assigned service jobs.
- View customer details required to perform assigned work.
- Update service progress.
- Enter technical findings.
- Record work completed.
- Add products and parts used.
- Enter service charges and collection information where authorized.
- Record handover information.
- Submit daily work reports.
- Submit new service requests.
- Submit TA/DA expenses.
- View their own submitted expense claims and approval status.

Technicians must not delete records or approve their own submitted service requests, expense claims, or schedules.

Every important update must be recorded in the activity log and notify Admin.

