# 16. Security & Data Integrity

Security is mandatory.

- Enforce role permissions on the server, not only in the frontend.
- Validate all user input.
- Protect against unauthorized record access.
- Secure file uploads.
- Use parameterized database queries or a safe ORM.
- Protect authentication and password reset flows.
- Use expiring email verification tokens.
- Add rate limiting where appropriate.
- Keep credentials and secrets out of source control.
- Log important changes.
- Restrict sensitive financial information to authorized roles.
- Provide a backup and recovery strategy.
- Avoid permanent deletion of important business records; prefer authorized archival or soft deletion.
- Keep audit history for sensitive operations.

